# Backend-specific ignores.
#
# The repository root .gitignore already covers everything here except the last
# two sections. This file is deliberate redundancy, for two reasons:
#
#   1. Secrets. backend/.env holds the real database URL. If the root file is
#      ever edited, moved, or this directory is copied elsewhere, that ignore
#      must not travel away with it. Defense in depth on the one file whose
#      accidental commit cannot be undone by deleting it in a later commit.
#   2. Locality. Someone working only in backend/ can see what is ignored
#      without reading a file two directories up.
#
# Nested .gitignore rules resolve relative to THIS directory, and a nested file
# can re-ignore something the root un-ignored. Hence the explicit
# `!.env.example` below — without it this file would shadow the root's negation
# and hide the committed template.

# ---------- Secrets (the reason this file exists) ----------
# .env.example is the committed template and contains no real values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------- Virtual environment ----------
# Recreated from requirements.txt; never committed.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---------- Bytecode and packaging artifacts ----------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ---------- Test and tooling caches ----------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
# import-linter currently writes a self-ignoring .gitignore into its own cache
# directory, so this line is belt-and-braces rather than a fix for a gap.
.import_linter_cache/

# ---------- Not covered by the root file ----------
# Local scratch databases. The real database is hosted Postgres on Supabase;
# any .db/.sqlite3 here is something someone created while experimenting and is
# never part of the project.
*.db
*.sqlite3

# Ad-hoc log output, e.g. from redirecting uvicorn or alembic.
*.log
